A standard chest X-ray projects the three-dimensional structures of the chest onto a two-dimensional surface. The orientation shown here, displaying the anterior-posterior relationship of the ribs and spine with the lungs and heart in between, corresponds to the **coronal plane** (frontal plane). It does not represent a transverse/axial slice. Therefore, it is not a transverse plane.

